    },
    {
      "id": "t-QB4-fig",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2307.0,
      "y": 2531.0,
      "width": 664.3,
      "height": 195.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "frame-QB4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1056023994,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1888033564,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "today                                proposed split (inside the skill dir)\n────────────────────────             ─────────────────────────────────────\nbuild.py  ~2,500 lines               build.py     parser + assembly  (~1,100)\n  parser        ~500                 assets/board.css   the page CSS\n  CSS template  ~700                 assets/board.js    comments + drawer + terminal\n  page JS       ~800                 → build.py READS and INLINES them at build\n  index/render  ~500                 → output stays ONE self-contained board.html\n                                     → node --check / a linter can run on board.js directly\n\nshould it move to haichat-board?  NO —\n  the grammar must live where every SPACE carries it: Tools (a submodule of\n  every SPACE). haichat-board is ONE consumer importing it (QE3 Law). Move it\n  there and offline builds + serve.py + other SPACEs all lose their parser.",
      "originalText": "today                                proposed split (inside the skill dir)\n────────────────────────             ─────────────────────────────────────\nbuild.py  ~2,500 lines               build.py     parser + assembly  (~1,100)\n  parser        ~500                 assets/board.css   the page CSS\n  CSS template  ~700                 assets/board.js    comments + drawer + terminal\n  page JS       ~800                 → build.py READS and INLINES them at build\n  index/render  ~500                 → output stays ONE self-contained board.html\n                                     → node --check / a linter can run on board.js directly\n\nshould it move to haichat-board?  NO —\n  the grammar must live where every SPACE carries it: Tools (a submodule of\n  every SPACE). haichat-board is ONE consumer importing it (QE3 Law). Move it\n  there and offline builds + serve.py + other SPACEs all lose their parser.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
